# @@@AX25_SYSCONFDIR@@@/axports
#
# The format of this file is:
#
# name callsign speed paclen window description
#
# The name is what a program passes to say which port it wants, and which
# backend serves it follows from the name:
#
#   - a name in ax25netd_agwpe.conf is served by ax25netd.  "radio0" is the first
#     channel of upstream radio0, "radio0:1" its second, and so on.  The
#     name is the upstream's name from ax25netd_agwpe.conf, not the name of the
#     program behind it - an upstream called radio0 that is a Direwolf is
#     still "radio0" here, and calling the entry "direwolf" or "vhfdrop"
#     is what makes a bind land on a port nobody serves.  An "agwpe-"
#     prefix is accepted and stripped, for a file that also has kernel
#     interfaces of the same name.
#   - a name in wampes.conf is served by that node.  "wampes" is the node
#     itself; "wampes:hfb" pins one of its ports.
#   - anything else is a kernel AX.25 interface, and the callsign has to
#     be the one that interface carries.
#
# The callsign is the default source call of the port, paclen the default
# packet size (mtu), window the default MAXFRAME.  It is also how a
# program names the port: it lands in the first digipeater slot of the
# bind address, so a program that put a callsign there which no line below
# carries is naming a port that does not exist.
#
# The WAMPES node needs only the node-wide line: a port on the node (xnet,
# hfb, 70cm, ...) is named by a "wampes:<port>" name, and one that has no
# entry of its own is accepted under that line and routed to whatever port
# is actually reachable.  To always mean one specific port, give the
# "wampes:<port>" name its own line and callsign - the explicit entry wins
# over the fallback.

#radio0		DL1AAA	9600	256	7	ax25netd_agwpe.conf upstream radio0, channel 0
#radio0:1	DL1AAA-1	9600	256	7	ax25netd_agwpe.conf upstream radio0, channel 1
#radio0:2	DL1AAA-2	9600	256	7	ax25netd_agwpe.conf upstream radio0, channel 2
#wampes		DL9SAU-0	9600	256	7	WAMPES node
#wampes:hfb	DL9SAU-1	9600	256	7	WAMPES node, port hfb (pinned by its own call)
#bpq0		DL9SAU-2	9600	256	7	kernel AX.25 interface bpq0
